IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wica-types`

-- Work Injury Compensation Act 2019 — GOAL 4: WHO IS PAID, WHEN IS IT A
-- DISCHARGE, HOW MUCH INTEREST, AND WHEN MUST MONEY COME BACK?
--
-- ss 18-23 (payment, deposit, relatives, discharge, no contracting out),
-- s 59 (interest), and the refund powers of ss 16(5)-(8), 17(5)-(7),
-- 34M(5)-(7), 34N(6)-(8) and 54(4). Part 3A applies ss 18-21 and 23 to
-- platform operators and workers with the words exchanged (s 34B(b)); the
-- rules below are written once for both.
--
-- Source: ../source/WICA2019.txt lines 714-945, 3059-3071.

§ `Goal 4 — payment`

§§ `Whom the insurer pays (s 18(2)-(3))`

-- s 18(2): the employer's insurer "must pay the amount ... within the
-- prescribed time: (a) unless paragraph (b), (c), (d) or (e) applies, to the
-- employee; (b) unless paragraph (c), (d) or (e) applies, to the public
-- trustee if — (i) the compensation is in respect of permanent incapacity or
-- current incapacity ...; and (ii) the employee is below 18 years of age; (c)
-- where the employee has died — to the executor or administrator ..., if the
-- employer's insurer has been informed that an executor or administrator has
-- been appointed; (d) where the employee lacks capacity ... — [to a donee or
-- deputy]; (e) where the Commissioner so directs under section 20 — to any
-- relative ...". s 18(3): a direction to deposit under s 21 is obeyed.
-- (c), (d) and (e) carry no order among themselves; (e) is a direction, and
-- is read as prevailing where given.
-- A dead employee with no executor known, or an incapable one with no donee or
-- deputy, has no payee under s 18(2) until the Commissioner directs (s 20,
-- s 21) — the Act's own answer.
@ref s 18(2), (3)
GIVEN f IS A `Payee facts`
GIVETH A Payee
`whom the insurer pays, under s 18:` f MEANS
    BRANCH IF f's `the Commissioner has directed a deposit`
              THEN `a deposit with the Commissioner`                              -- (3)
           IF f's `the Commissioner has directed payment to relatives`
              THEN `the claimant's relatives, as the Commissioner directs`        -- (e)
           IF f's `the claimant has died`
              THEN IF f's `an executor or administrator is known to be appointed`
                   THEN `the executor or administrator`                           -- (c)
                   ELSE `no one until the Commissioner directs (s 20, s 21)`
           IF f's `the claimant lacks capacity in property and affairs`
              THEN IF f's `a donee or deputy with power to receive the payment`
                   THEN `the donee or deputy`                                     -- (d)
                   ELSE `no one until the Commissioner directs (s 20, s 21)`
           IF f's `the claimant is below 18` AND f's `for permanent or current incapacity`
              THEN `the Public Trustee`                                           -- (b)
           OTHERWISE `the claimant`                                               -- (a)

§§ `Whom the employer pays, or must deposit with (s 19)`

-- s 19(2): "Unless the Commissioner directs otherwise under section 20, an
-- employer must deposit ... with the Commissioner: (a) any compensation ... if
-- — (i) the employee has died; or (ii) the employee lacks capacity ...; (b)
-- any compensation ... in respect of any permanent incapacity or current
-- incapacity ..., if the employee is below 18 years of age; (c) any
-- compensation ... that the Commissioner directs the employer to deposit under
-- section 21." s 19(1): otherwise "(a) to the employee; or (b) where the
-- Commissioner so directs under section 20 — to any relative".
@ref s 19(1), (2)
GIVEN f IS A `Payee facts`
GIVETH A Payee
`whom the employer pays, under s 19:` f MEANS
    BRANCH IF f's `the Commissioner has directed payment to relatives`
              THEN `the claimant's relatives, as the Commissioner directs`        -- (1)(b); "unless the Commissioner directs otherwise"
           IF     f's `the claimant has died`
               OR f's `the claimant lacks capacity in property and affairs`
               OR (f's `the claimant is below 18` AND f's `for permanent or current incapacity`)
               OR f's `the Commissioner has directed a deposit`
              THEN `a deposit with the Commissioner`                              -- (2)(a)-(c)
           OTHERWISE `the claimant`                                               -- (1)(a)

§§ `Discharge (s 22), and no contracting out (s 23)`

-- s 22(1)-(3): a receipt by a person paid in accordance with s 18(2), 19(1)
-- or 21(2)(a)-(d), or by the Commissioner for a deposit, "is a sufficient
-- discharge"; a payment "made in contravention of [those provisions] is
-- deemed not to be a discharge". Applies despite the law on estates, the
-- Mental Capacity Act 2008 and the Insurance Act 1966 (s 22(5)).
@ref s 22(1)-(3)
GIVEN `the person actually paid` IS A Payee
      `the payee the Act names`  IS A Payee
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paying` `the person actually paid` `discharges the compensation, the Act naming` `the payee the Act names` IF
        NOT `the payee the Act names` EQUALS `no one until the Commissioner directs (s 20, s 21)`
    AND `the person actually paid` EQUALS `the payee the Act names`

-- s 23(1): "Subject to sections 51 and 52(c), any contract or agreement by
-- which an employee relinquishes any right of compensation ... is void insofar
-- as it purports to remove or reduce the liability of any person to pay
-- compensation". s 23(2): compensation is not assignable, attachable or
-- subject to set-off.
@ref s 23(1)
GIVEN `relinquishes or reduces a right to compensation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a settlement recorded under s 51 or s 52(c)`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement is void under s 23(1):` `relinquishes or reduces a right to compensation` `, recorded as a settlement:` `a settlement recorded under s 51 or s 52(c)` IF
        `relinquishes or reduces a right to compensation`
    AND NOT `a settlement recorded under s 51 or s 52(c)`

@ref s 23(2)
GIVEN `an assignment, attachment or set-off of compensation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(2) forbids it:` `an assignment, attachment or set-off of compensation` IF
    `an assignment, attachment or set-off of compensation`

§§ `Interest on late payment (s 59)`

-- s 59(1): interest at the prescribed rate on compensation not paid or
-- deposited in time. s 59(2): "The total amount of interest ... must not
-- exceed 50% of the amount of compensation that the person has failed to pay
-- or deposit within the required time." The rate is in regulations: the
-- interest at that rate is an input. s 59(4): the Commissioner may waive or
-- remit it.
@ref s 59(1)-(2)
GIVEN `interest at the prescribed rate` IS A NUMBER
      `the compensation paid late`      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the interest payable, at the prescribed rate` `interest at the prescribed rate` `, on late compensation of` `the compensation paid late` MEANS
    IF   `interest at the prescribed rate` GREATER THAN `the compensation paid late` TIMES 50%
    THEN `the compensation paid late` TIMES 50%
    ELSE `interest at the prescribed rate`

§§ `Refunds and reimbursements (ss 16(5)-(8), 17(5)-(7), 34M(5)-(7), 34N(6)-(8), 54(4))`

-- ss 16(5), 17(5), 34M(5), 34N(6): the Commissioner MAY order the claimant to
-- reimburse or refund a payment if "(a) the claim ... is withdrawn, and is not
-- resumed, under section 41; (b) an order of refusal of compensation has been
-- made or has taken effect ...; or (c) the payment was made on the basis of
-- any error or any false or misleading information." Their subsections (6)
-- (or (7)): only if "(a) the payer applies to the Commissioner ... within the
-- prescribed time ...; and (b) the claimant has been given a reasonable
-- opportunity to make representations". s 16(7): never a payment the employer
-- must make under the Employment of Foreign Manpower Act 1990.
-- s 54(4): on a review order, a refund of an overpayment made on the basis of
-- an error or false or misleading information.
DECLARE `Refund facts` HAS
    `the claim was withdrawn and not resumed`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `an order of refusal has been made or taken effect`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid on the basis of an error or false or misleading information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the payer applied in time, in the required form`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claimant had a reasonable opportunity to make representations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a medical payment the employer owes under the Employment of Foreign Manpower Act 1990` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref ss 16(5)-(7), 17(5)-(6), 34M(5)-(6), 34N(6)-(7)
GIVEN f IS A `Refund facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner may order a refund or reimbursement to the payer:` f IF
        `a ground in (5)`
    AND "(6)(a)" ... f's `the payer applied in time, in the required form`
    AND "(6)(b)" ... f's `the claimant had a reasonable opportunity to make representations`
    AND NOT "s 16(7)" ... f's `a medical payment the employer owes under the Employment of Foreign Manpower Act 1990`
    WHERE
        `a ground in (5)` MEANS
                "(a)" ... f's `the claim was withdrawn and not resumed`
            ..  "(b)" ... f's `an order of refusal has been made or taken effect`
            OR  "(c)" ... f's `paid on the basis of an error or false or misleading information`

@ref s 54(4)
GIVEN f IS A `Refund facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Commissioner may order an overpayment refunded on review:` f IF
    f's `paid on the basis of an error or false or misleading information`
